{
 "item": "L6",
 "kind": "capture",
 "oracle": "trial site, Blocks Probe, a new Shape, unsaved",
 "capturedAt": "2026-11-07",
 "question": "An Animation set on a phone: can it be added, does it count as an override, does it stay on the phone",
 "how": "Named presses with an on-top check. The Remove icon is 0 opacity until hovered and pressed all the same. Rows are read by their button text, label dots by computed style. Left by Exit Without Saving.",
 "add": {
  "disabled": true,
  "svg": "rgb(183, 183, 183)",
  "cursor": "default",
  "withRows": true,
  "desktop": "on, svg rgb(14, 14, 14), cursor pointer"
 },
 "rules": [
  "On a phone the + is off, on an empty list and on a list with rows, and an empty list has no Press + to get started.",
  "The phone button is on the Design tab, not on the Animation tab.",
  "Rows are shared when added or removed. Remove on a phone takes the row from both layouts, with own values or not. Add only exists on desktop.",
  "A row opened on a phone can be set. A value set there is the phones alone, key by key: Opacity 37 on the phone leaves desktop on 100 and its preset; Rotate 30 on desktop then reaches the phone, whose Opacity stays 37.",
  "The label of a value the phone set is dotted in the row editor: Opacity, Rotate, Delay. A pick on the phone dots all five End labels. In the list the row gets a black dotted line under its icon, read in screenshots. Tabs get no dot, and the Design tab shows none for it.",
  "Such a value lights the phone button. Reset all overrides takes the phone back to desktop, Push to desktop gives desktop the phones values, trigger too; then the button is off.",
  "A pick on the phone changes the phone row only (Lift 0.35s on the phone, Grow 0.5s on desktop). A changed trigger too: On Press on the phone, On Hover on desktop, and that row goes after the other rows on the phone.",
  "Preview on a phone plays the phones values (Rotate 45, Opacity 40) and on desktop desktops.",
  "After removing the row that held the only own value, the button stays on: read three times, and only Reset all overrides turned it off."
 ],
 "inferred": [
  "After a pick, Ease, Duration and the other Timing labels are dotted: End was read, Timing was not.",
  "Two rows with changed triggers: their order between them.",
  "A desktop pick on a row with phone values keeps those values.",
  "Remove on desktop of a row with phone values does not light the button.",
  "Copy Properties on a phone.",
  "A page in preview mode at phone width: ours plays the phones row, the oracles was read only by the Preview buttons.",
  "Reset on a field in a phones row writes the default as the phones own, as Design rows do.",
  "A row delay on desktop: the list was read with a delay only on a phone."
 ],
